\par\par \b \uc2  Chile's Peso Ends Lower, Again Tracks Brazil's Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2002\par 19:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- Chile's peso retreated against the dollar Monday, falling for the second session in a row after the Brazilian real weakened intraday. \par \par \uc2  Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at CLP700.80 to the dollar, compared with CLP697.00 Friday. \par \par \uc2  The real weakened again despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as international credit for companies who need to settle foreign debts failed to materialize despite the record $30 billion the International Monetary Fund has promised Brazil. \par \par \uc2  Monday, companies had to buy dollars in the spot market, thus pressuring the peso. \par \par \uc2  However, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did manage to stabilize \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso above technical support around CLP701.50, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But the real is having a more immediate impact than technical trading, they added. \par \par \uc2  Brazil had been seeking IMF help after the popularity of leftist candidates in the run-up to that country's October presidential elections caused investors to flee the region, dragging down other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Chilean peso, with it. \par \par \uc2  Strongly influenced by the wavering fortune of the real, the peso has fluctuated largely in a CLP690-700 range, though dropping as far as close to CLP710 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Even after the IMF promised Brazil additional help last week, traders doubted the peso would recover to a higher level than CLP685 in a short time. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546;\par     stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com\par     (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020812dy8c000zt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
