\par\par \b \uc2  Chile's Peso Close To Historic Lows, But No Worries \b0\par\par\uc2  By Stephan Kueffner \par \uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2002\par 18:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- After breaching technical support Wednesday, Chile's peso is once again poised to test historic lows against the dollar, but not even Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks worried. \par \par \uc2  Hit primarily by the fallout from troubled Brazil, the peso needs to lose only another 2.5% versus the dollar to reach Oct. 2001's historic low of CLP718.70. But Chilean inflation is under control and a weak peso will bring smiles to exporters - and help Chile overcome low growth. \par \par \uc2  That will keep fear of imported inflation at bay "as long as the peso continues to weaken in tandem with other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," helping Chilean products stay competitive, said Clyde Wardle, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at HSBC in New York. \par \par \uc2  Trading at or below CLP702 a dollar early Wednesday, the peso fell through technical support traders had put at CLP701.50. \par \par \uc2  While it recovered in intraday trading, traders said it could fall to CLP710 easily and then move on towards the historic low. \par \par \uc2  "The price of the dollar isn't excessive considering the effect uncertainty in Brazil and the international bourses are having on capital flows" to Latin America, said analyst Cristian Gardewerg at Santander Investment. \par \par \uc2  The peso has been trading in a CLP690-700 range for a number of weeks. \par \par \uc2  It has been at that low level due to worries concerning its exposure to crisis-stricken neighbor Argentina and, above all, troubled Brazil, South America's biggest economy. Several major Chilean companies have invested heavily in those countries. \par \par \uc2  Apparently, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't worried. July 11, it surprised markets with an unexpectedly large 75-basis-point rate cut to 3.25% from 4%. \par \par \uc2  However, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall to near historic lows would certainly alert it, analysts said. Knowing that, traders will be cautious once it gets below CLP715, they added. \par \par \uc2  "The peso will remain volatile but it will reach a maximum low around CLP715 a dollar because the market knows that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could react at any time then," said Erick Haindl, economist at Universidad Gabriela Mistral in Santiago. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Unlikely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso might even go to CLP720 if the international stock market\par crisis continues, but even there "the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't have to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly and sell its reserve dollars," said trader Cristian\par Donoso Banco de \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Before \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  outright, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could still let off a\par loud warning shot by offering dollar-denominated two-to-four year\par securities - so-called PRDs - that buyers can use to hedge against\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses, while injecting dollar liquidity, analysts said. It\par last announced devaluation-inspired PRDs last August.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank itself believes the peso's weakness is a passing thing, it\par said recently. September and December are the next months PRDs will be\par on offer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If and when calm returns to international markets - in Latin American\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well as major stock markets - the peso could easily return\par back to CLP650-670, economists said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, that's unlikely before October's Brazilian presidential\par elections, where the popularity of left-of-center candidates has been\par enough to spark fear - and major selling - in the markets, they added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The weakening of Latin America's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reflects investment moving\par to Asia and Eastern Europe, analysts said. For Chile, this will be of\par little concern as the country is still able to reliably pull in outside\par capital, HSBC's Wardle said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546;\par chiledowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020724dy7o0011m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
