\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bank Ends  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Policy Jan 1 \b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2001\par 16:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president, Carlos Massad, said Friday the bank won't directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after Dec. 31, ending a policy in effect since August. \par \par \uc2  On Aug. 16, the bank said it was prepared to pump up to $2 billion in reserves into the market by the end of the year. In the weeks leading up to the announcement, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed whole percentage points in single trading sessions, largely due to pressures linked to Argentina's economic crisis. \par \par \uc2  Massad said Friday that the bank sold about 40% of the total $2 billion since the policy was launched. \par \par \uc2  Chile's peso, which was trading firmer early Friday, changed direction and is slipping weaker on the news. \par \par \uc2  Chile's peso finished weaker Friday, at CLP660.50 to the dollar, reversing significant gains made early in the session. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the peso slipped primarily on news that the bank won't inject any more dollars into the market, but also on a bit of rate cut speculation sparked by some of Massad's comments. \par \par \uc2  When asked about local interest rates Friday, Massad suggested the bank might consider lowering its benchmark monetary policy rate, currently set at a nominal 6.50%. \par \par \uc2  "If inflation remains stable and external risks continue to be absorbed, we think that could open up possibilities for additional steps in the area of monetary policy," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president said. \par \par \uc2  Tomas Flores, an economist with Chile's Liberty and Development think tank, sees Friday's rate cut speculation as overblown. \par \par \uc2  Flores expects the bank to wait and see if local and international growth continues to decline before deciding whether the economy needs more stimulus. Even so, controlled inflation does give the bank room to trim should they choose to go that route, he says. \par \par \uc2  A few months ago, rising international oil prices and a falling local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were threatening to stir up inflation in Chile. But since early October, those pressures have begun to ease. \par \par \uc2  Weak domestic demand has also helped keep consumer prices in check. Economists see zero inflation for December, which would be a repeat of November's performance. \par \par \uc2  The underlying pressure on Chile's peso has also dissipated, at least temporarily. \par \par \uc2  The peso, which depreciated as much as 20% against the dollar this year, began to rebound in October as prices for copper, Chile's No. 1 export product, staged a meek recovery. A round of production cuts, while not convincing enough to override weak demand for the metal, at least fanned hopes that prices will respond quickly when demand does pick up. \par \par \uc2  Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also began to cut loose in October from the turmoil in neighboring Argentina. By last week, the peso had firmed to levels not seen since July. \par \par \uc2  But while pressures are continuing to ease, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves the right to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again should circumstances spin out of control, Massad said Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  swore off market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and floated the peso two years ago, finally putting in place an inflation targeting monetary policy system that was years in the making. \par \par \uc2  Web site {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcentral.cl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bcentral.cl}}}\par \par \uc2  -Andrea Welsh, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8547; chile@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011228dxcs000s7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
