\par\par \b \uc2  Chile Cenbank cuts 2002 growth estimate to 3-4 pct. \b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2001\par 00:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Chile, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday cut its 2002 economic growth forecast to between 3 percent and 4 percent from a previous forecast of 5 percent due to the worsening global economic outlook after the Sept. 11 attacks in the United States. \par \par \uc2  "Consensus estimates point to a downward revision of about one percentage point in the growth of Chile's trade partners toward the end of 2002," the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement following its monthly monetary policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  The institution opted to keep interest rates unchanged at 6.5 percent because of inflationary pressures caused in part by a sharp depreciation of the peso. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its inflationary target of between 2 percent and 4 percent and said it will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to bolster the peso. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-driven economy grew 3.4 percent in the January to July period after posting 5.4 percent growth in all of 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011009dxa90164w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
