\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso falters despite Cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2001\par 21:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 13 (Reuters) - The Chilean peso fell slightly on Thursday despite a small \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to break the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed at 680.50/681.00 to the U.S. dollar, losing 0.2 percent from Wednesday's close of 678.50/679.00 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Trading was volatile and confused as players remained dazed by the devastating plane attacks in the United States on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected about $25 million into the market, according to a Reuters survey of traders. \par \par \uc2  Since mid-August, when the institution announced it would sell up to $2 billion from its reserves to prop up the peso, it has sold an estimated $91.5 million in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The peso has depreciated about 15 percent so far this year on regional woes. \par \par \uc2  Chile's stock market closed on Tuesday shortly after the attacks in the United States. Trading resumed on Wednesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010913dx9d00u3y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
