\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In Mkt At CLP663/Dlr -Trader \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2001\par 17:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  31/08/01 15-32G \par \par \uc2  1532GMT \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  returned to sell dollars directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday when Chile's peso hit CLP663.00 to the dollar at about midsession, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped to CLP659.50 within 15 minutes of the sale, at 1530 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Traders didn't know the amount the bank sold on the market. \par \par \uc2  A local trader said the bank stopped selling dollars after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to CLP659.50, but added that it could return at any moment. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened Friday's session at CLP660.90 to the dollar, a hair stronger than Thursday's close of CLP661.50, but then weakened steadily until the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at CLP663.00. \par \par \uc2  At 1600 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had lost some of its recent steam, weakening to CLP660.80 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  This marks the second time this week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. On Tuesday, the bank sold dollars on the market when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit CLP666.00, and stopped at CLP660.00, traders said. \par \par \uc2  While the bank confirmed its Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it referred markets to its international reserves report, due out on Sept. 7, to determine the total amount. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced that it was prepared to use up to $2 billion of its foreign reserves to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This week is the first time the bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since it floated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1999. \par \par \uc2  -By Christen A. Jamar, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; chile@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010831dx8v000xy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
