\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Chile cenbank move boosts peso - for now. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Gabriela Donoso \par \uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2001\par 00:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 6 (Reuters) - A Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to break the peso's fall will reap short-term success but the determining factor for the peso is the regional economic outlook, analysts said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  As the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit record lows on Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would inject $1 billion into the financial market by issuing dollar-denominated promissory notes over the next six months. The notes act as insurance for banks against financial losses caused by exposure to dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  "This announcement took the market by surprise, which makes me think that it will at least bring to an end the sharp decline," said Alejandro Fernandez, analyst with Gemines consultancy in Santiago. \par \par \uc2  "What is not clear is whether or not the amount announced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sufficient to break that tendency," he added. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time the institution stepped in to influence the exchange rate since it floated the peso in 1999. \par \par \uc2  The move aims to soften the impact on the peso of neighbor Argentina's chronic political and economic troubles, which have helped drag the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  11 percent lower so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement, the peso firmed almost 1 percent to close on Friday at 642.20/642.50 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had plunged to a record low of 649 pesos earlier on Thursday amid rumors that Argentine president Fernando de la Rua was about to resign. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR FEVER \par \par \uc2  Ongoing fears that Argentina will abandon its dollar-pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system or default on its debt have led to a feverish race among Chilean players to acquire dollars. \par \par \uc2  However, economists say the Chilean market is overreacting. \par \par \uc2  "My opinion is that Argentina is not going to default nor will it have a major crisis. Everything will be done to ensure that doesn't happen. The authorities would have to be totally inept to let things get to that point," said Guillermo Patillo, economist at the University of Santiago. \par \par \uc2  Argentina, Latin America's No. 3 economy, will continue to be key influence on regional markets through to year-end, analyst said. But they say there is no reason why the Chilean peso should tumble dramatically as a result. \par \par \uc2  "We are optimistic about Argentina. I think it is very unlikely for there to be a default or for the (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) convertibility system to be dropped in the short term," said Sergio Quintana, economist with Forecast consultants. \par \par \uc2  The peso has fallen on more than just regional turmoil. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also teetered from a series of domestic interest rate cuts earlier this year to rekindle spending amid a broader economic slowdown. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark lending rate now stands at 3.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The anticipation of lower economic activity and therefore of another cut in rates, are factors that have affected the exchange rate," Fernandez said. \par \par \uc2  Some traders interpreted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a sign that it set the 650 pesos-mark as the ceiling for the exchange rate and would actively defend that level. \par \par \uc2  But in theory, there is no limit. Some analysts see the peso hitting 700 pesos to the dollar if speculation is not restrained. \par \par \uc2  "It is impossible to say how high the dollar will go in Chile. It could reach the sky," Quintana quipped. \par \par \uc2  $1 = 642.5 Chilean pesos. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010706dx76007es\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
