\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cenbank in $1 bln  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Paulina Modiano \par \uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2001\par 00:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it would inject $1 billion into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the battered peso , its first such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1999. \par \par \uc2  The move came as several regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  buckled under pressure from the Argentine economic crisis. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday pledged $6 billion to defend the real. \par \par \uc2  Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Carlos Massad told Reuters his institution will issue dollar-denominated promissory notes over the next six months as a hedging mechanism, effectively backing up commercial banks' dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  "Given the turbulence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, there is strong demand for this type of coverage instrument," Massad said in an interview. \par \par \uc2  News of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit after markets had closed but caused \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to perk up immediately, gaining eight pesos or 1.2 percent in after-hours trading, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Details of the transaction will be made public on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Chilean peso has hit historical lows in recent sessions in reaction to political and economic tension in neighboring Argentina, Latin America's third-largest economy. \par \par \uc2  After faltering from a series of domestic interest rate cuts earlier in the year, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank to fresh lows this week on rumors, later denied, that Argentine President Fernando de la Rua was about to resign. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed on Thursday at 648.50/648.80 pesos to the dollar, down 0.96 percent from Wednesday's close and down over 11 percent since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  Massad said the $1 billion worth of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes, known locally as PRDs, would be injected into the market over and above the $1.5 billion already circulating in the market. \par \par \uc2  The institution will therefore have issued a total of $2.5 billion in PRD by year end. \par \par \uc2  The first $500 million will be placed as of July 9, he said. \par \par \uc2  NO MORE HANDS-OFF \par \par \uc2  Since 1999, when Chile adopted a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Before 1999, it frequently stepped in to buy and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to keep the exchange rate within a target range. \par \par \uc2  Last month, however, Massad told markets the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has the power to step in to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The PRD is one of the instruments the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has at its disposal to influence the exchange rate without directly withdrawing from its reserves. \par \par \uc2  Massad said he did not expect the announced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have a direct effect on the exchange rate but said it would provide some relief from pressure caused by regional instability. \par \par \uc2  "The situation in Brazil demonstrates how the turbulence is not internal but is affecting several markets and diverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it would spend $6 billion by the end of the year to shore up the beleaguered real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The strong dollar in Chile has spawned fears of high inflation, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pegged at 3.4 percent for 2001. But Massad ruled out inflationary pressure. \par \par \uc2  "So far, we have not seen any effect on inflation," he said. \par \par \uc2  Inflation in June was 0.1 percent, down from 0.4 percent in May due to falling oil prices. January-June inflation was 1.5 percent, according to the state statistics office. \par \par \uc2  Massad said Chilean authorities were closely monitoring Argentina, whose economy has been stalled for three years, prompting investors to doubt its ability to pay back its massive debt. \par \par \uc2  "What we want is for Argentina to recover and grow again. That would be the best thing that could happen to strengthen growth in Chile too," he said. \par \par \uc2  Chile recovered last year from an 11-month recession to post 5.4 percent economic growth. But low prices for copper, the country's top export, and a global slowdown have led to a slowdown this year. \par \par \uc2  First-quarter growth was 3.3 percent. In May, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its 2001 growth forecast to 4.3 percent from 5.6 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx7500570\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
