\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's cenbank says may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2001\par 19:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, June 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday said it has the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the local peso, driven to historic lows on fears of instability in Argentina and Brazil, from depreciating further. \par \par \uc2  The peso sank to record lows this week after Argentina announced it would exclude exports from its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg to the dollar, seen by the Chilean market as a "hidden devaluation." \par \par \uc2  A surprise cut in interest rates last week and a recent decline in Brazil's real also helped drive the peso lower. \par \par \uc2  "The market will have to decide where to set the price of the dollar, but I have always said that in exceptional circumstances the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Carlos Massad told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed on Wednesday at 624.00/624.30 pesos to the dollar, making for a depreciation of 2.6 percent in a little over a week and 8.2 percent so far this year. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciated 7.7 percent in all of 2000. \par \par \uc2  Until 1999, when Chile adopted a free-floating peso, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently stepped in to buy and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to keep the exchange rate within a target range. \par \par \uc2  Massad said it would warn markets ahead of time if it decides to return to that kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Argentine government on Friday announced changes to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, varying the peso's exchange rate for importers and exporters in a bid to cheapen exports and pull the economy out of a three-year stagnation. \par \par \uc2  Massad dismissed fears that the measures would hurt the Chilean economy but said the country could be dragged down along with other emerging markets if Argentina eventually defaults on its debt. \par \par \uc2  "Even though now we are seen as distinct (from the rest of the region), my fear is that we won't be distinct enough," he said. \par \par \uc2  Massad said the Chilean economy, which last year recovered from an 11-month recession to post 5.4 percent growth, may grow less than 4.3 percent this year. Last month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed its 2001 growth forecast to 4.3 percent from 5.6 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6k017s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
