\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk/GDP -3: No  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  In 6 Months \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1999\par 18:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In a chart accompanying the release of Massad's speech, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it expects consumer prices to rise by 3.0% during the current year. In the period January through August, the consumer price index rose by 1.3%. \par \par \uc2  Chile's economy contracted by 2.9% in the first half of the year, compared to the same period a year earlier. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it expects the country's GDP to grow by between 2.5% and 3.5% during the second half of the year. \par \par \uc2  Massad laid a large part of the blame for the economic downturn on the financial crisis in Asia, which has been a key market for Chilean exports in recent years. A prolonged drought, macroeconomic problems in Brazil and a sharp increase in crude oil prices all added to the country's difficulties, Massad said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president said the projected economic rebound will be driven by an increase in domestic demand. Net external demand could increase moderately next year due to a projected 16% increase in imports, offset somewhat by a reduction in the rate of growth of copper exports. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president said the higher import levels will come as a result of companies rebuilding diminished inventory levels and responding to stronger domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  Exports of goods are projected to grow by 9.0% this year, followed by a 5.0% increase during 2000. Copper exports are seen growing by 13% during 1999 and by 2.0% during the following year. Non-copper exports are projected to increase by 6.5% in both 1999 and 2000. \par \par \uc2  No estimates for exports of services were provided. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said that it expects gross capital formation to equal 27.5% of GDP this year, growing to 28.5% during the year 2000. \par \par \uc2  In his speech, Massad referred to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision last week to suspend its formal policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when the price of the dollar exceeds the limits of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band. \par \par \uc2  Massad said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets during the last six months. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-09-99 \par \par \uc2  1648GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9806jw5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
