\par\par \b \uc2  Chile  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  sells dollars to halt peso fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 1999\par 15:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Feb 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, selling dollars to stop the peso from trading too close to the pyschological 500 barrier, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The peso moved back to 496.00-497.00 after reaching 498 per dollar after almost an hour's trading. The peso closed Friday at 495.20/495.70 per dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chile's spot peso\tab   has been under intense pressure in recent sessions as corporate dollar demand has soared and the market has seen jitters because of the financial crisis in Brazil.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Friday, Chile's peso dropped again when Ecuador stopped using trading bands, which saw the sucre decline sharply.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said they did not immediately know how many dollars the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had injected into the system, but noted the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the peso fell to 498.30/498.80.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is selling to try to bring the price down and although it had immediate effect, the peso could fall again if the amounts are not substantial, given the constant demand," one dealer told Reuters. ((Froilan Romero, Santiago newsroom +562 699-5595 ext 210)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2f04l5s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\p