\par\par \b \uc2  Latin American Markets -2: Brazil Leads Losses \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 22:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The following is a round-up of Latin American markets at 2030 GMT: \par \par \uc2  - Brazil's benchmark Bovespa plunged 15% just minutes before the close, activating the second circuit breaker of the day. The earlier halt in trading, after a fall of 10% minutes after the opening, failed to stop the index from falling below 5,000. \par \par \uc2  - Argentina's Merval index finished 46.38 points or 13.3% lower at 301.73. \par \par \uc2  - Mexico's IPC stock index finished 9.8% lower at 2856.10 points. The peso recovered slightly from its record low set earlier in the day of 10.70 to the dollar to close at 10.60. But the recovery was due to the fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $200 million in its habitual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction and took the unusual step of spending $278 million in open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's IPSA index of leading shares lost 7.4% of its value by close. The Chilean peso ended slightly down at 474.30 to the dollar amid reports the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - Venezuelan stocks closed 4.4% down, with the bolivar slightly weaker at a mid rate of 587.40 to the dollar. The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to believed to have sold between $30 million and $40 million supporting the bolivar. \par \par \uc2  - Colombia fared comparatively well, with the IBB index falling just 0.7% and the peso strengthening to 1493.06 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Emerging market debt continued its month-long downward slide. The\par benchmark Brazilian C-Bond was down 4 3/8 to 52 1/2 bid. At 1:30 p.m.\par EDT, the spread of the J.P. Morgan Emerging Markets Bond Index had\par widened nearly 300 basis points to 1761 basis points over U.S.\par Treasurys.\par -By Thomas Catan; 201-938-2225; thomas.catan@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-09-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2056GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1191 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9a07tej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
