\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  but peso ends off-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 21:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Aug 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso ended slightly weaker on Thursday against the dollar despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy about $110 million worth of pesos, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed at 473.70/474.00 per dollar, down from Wednesday's 473.30/473.60. \par \par \uc2  During Thursday's session, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dollars to buy pesos at a range of between 474.10 pesos and 474.40, traders said. One bank said the institution alone sold it $15 million worth of greenbacks. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimate the total amount sold to have been about $110 million. \par \par \uc2  Traders criticised the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calling them "too weak" for the current situation, which they said demands tougher measures. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  did trim losses in the last minutes of the session after banks dumped their excess dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  ((Froilan Romero, Santiago newsroom, +562 699-5595 x 212, fax +562 696-0161)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8r01nst\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
