\par\par \b \uc2  Chile's Peso Ends Weaker Amid Global Stock Market Declines \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 20:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended trading Thursday weaker against the U.S. dollar as key stock markets around the world were down sharply at GMT 1700, the closing time for local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range between 473.70 pesos and 474.30 pesos to the dollar. One U.S. dollar bought 473.70 pesos at the end of trading day, 40 centavos more than the previous session's closing price. \par \par \uc2  The trader said there was heavy pressure on the peso amid aggressive selling. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added, made two large dollar sales to buttress the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The bank came on strong, injecting dollars into the market," the trader said. An official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't comment on the reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The traded added that \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is being completely guided by foreign events. "Local news has been meaningless," the trader said. "The peso is immediately reacting to anything happening in financial markets abroad." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On debt markets, there was no trading in eight-year PRC bonds.\par   -By Felipe Ossa (562) 638 7472\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1801GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8r07bs6\par }\p