\par\par \b \uc2  D&P rates Chile $270 mln dlr-tied PRD notes A-plus. \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1998\par 18:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, July 16 (Reuters) - Duff and Phelps Credit Rating Co. on Thursday said it assigned an A-plus rating to the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's programme to issue $270 million in three-year, dollar-linked readjustable promissory notes (PRDs). \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed $30 million of the notes on July 9 at 6.51 percent at an initial spread of 111 basis points over three-year U.S. Treasury rates, Duff said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  The ratings outlook is stable, it said. \par \par \uc2  Because the PRDs are payable in pesos, their credit profile is similar to Chile's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , long-term debt rating of AA-minus, Duff said. \par \par \uc2  However, the rating is limited because interest and principal payments are linked to the exchange rate between the dollar and peso, it said. \par \par \uc2  The rating also reflects the PRDs' relatively small amounts and long maturities, which limit potential pressure arising in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market upon their redemption, it said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced June 25 that it would offer money market instruments linked to the dollar to give players the option of buying paper with a built-in hedge against the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. \par \par \uc2  The aim is to steady the skittish \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which has been seriously shaken up by the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  The institution plans to auction $30 million in PRDs every Tuesday and Thursday from July 9 to August 8 for a total of $270 million. \par \par \uc2  The notes are specifically designed to reduce banks' and dollar-indebted companies' demand in the spot market for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollars, Duff said. \par \par \uc2  Its reserves dropped in June by $1.32 billion to end the first half of the year at $15.55 billion. Traders attributed the fall to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the peso. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened sharply since November on expectations that the crisis will reduce revenues from exports. The peso traded today at 461.50/461.80 to the dollar, down sharply from around 415 last fall. \par \par \uc2  ((Tiffany Woods, Santiago newsroom, +562 699-5595 ext 212, +562 696-0161)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7g00t39\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
