\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Weaker Despite Reported  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1998\par 20:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended trading Wednesday weaker against the dollar despite reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range between 455.90 pesos and 456.50 pesos to the dollar. One dollar bought 456.50 pesos at the end of trading day, 70 centavos more than the previous session's closing price. \par \par \uc2  A trader with a local bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  felt compelled to step in to halt a steeper slide by the peso. A trader on the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money desk said it was against the institution's policy to comment on the report. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reportedly been selling dollars in recent weeks to deal with pressures related to Japan's precarious financial situation. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling today, but not as much as last week," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  On debt markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's eight-year PRC bonds were trading to yield 7.70% on an annual basis at the end of the day, compared to the previous session's 7.62% close. \par \par \uc2  -By William Hoke (562) 639 7895 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1840GMT \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020