\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Up After Reported  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 19:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended trading Monday slightly stronger against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said a trader with a Santiago bank. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range between 455.50 pesos and 455.90 pesos to the dollar. One dollar bought 455.50 pesos at the end of trading day, 25 centavos less than the previous session's closing price. \par \par \uc2  The trader said the peso started falling from the start of the three-hour session. He said a large dollar purchase by an unspecified U.S. bank put additional pressure on the peso, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to unload between $50 million and $100 million in dollars. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  found itself forced to defend its apparent ceiling of 456 pesos to the dollar. "If they didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar could go to maybe 460 (pesos) right away," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  On debt markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's eight-year PRC bonds were trading to yield 7.40% on an annual basis at the end of the day, compared to the previous session's 7.32% close. \par \par \uc2  By William Hoke (562) 639 7895 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones