\par\par \b \uc2  Chile stocks swing lower in kneejerk sell-off. \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 17:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, June 10 (Reuters) - Chile's key stock index swung lower early Wednesday in what traders said was a knee-jerk sell-off after Tuesday's sharp gains. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark index slumped 1.47 percent to 90.53 points, almost wiping out all the previous session gains when the blue-chip index jumped 2.03 percent. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's sharp leap came after the Chilean government announced plans to introduce three reforms to rejuvenate stock market trading. \par \par \uc2  "The euphoria of yesterday has fizzled out," one trader said. "The general feeling is that the reforms are not profound enough to bring about a real change in attitude about the (equity) market." \par \par \uc2  The government stimulus package includes two proposals to tweak capital gains tax rules on equities trading to favour more volume and a third plan to broaden the sphere of tax deductions on equity investments. \par \par \uc2  Other traders said the fall on Wall Street and the general downturn in Asian markets also hurt stock prices in Chile. \par \par \uc2  Chile's peso saw opening pressure, which brought \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers into the market selling an unspecified, "but not heavy" amount of dollars, one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the peso weakened to 455.80/456.10 per dollar. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged back to 455.70/456.00. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market for the past two months, holding the peso under a ceiling of 456.00 per dollar in an open stance to stabilise the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the grounds that letting it weaken could bring inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  ((Chris Aspin, Santiago newsroom +562 699-5595, ext 211)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a034nj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
