\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Stronger On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 1998\par 20:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended trading Monday stronger against the dollar following \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said a trader at a local bank. An official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't confirm or deny the reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range between 455.55 pesos and 455.80 pesos to the dollar. One dollar bought 455.55 pesos at the end of trading day, 15 centavos less than the previous session's closing price. \par \par \uc2  The trader said that impelling the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the peso was a boost in dollar demand amid tumult in Asian and Russian financial markets and a drop in copper prices. These events, he added, pushed the dollar's peso price to 455.80. "This (level) was just too high for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  As Chile's main export item, copper has a profound impact on the trade balance. In 1997, the base metal generated 40% of export revenues. Copper closed Monday at $0.762 a pound on the London Metals Exchange, from $0.764 the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The trader said continued uncertainty in Asia and weak copper prices will probably keep dragging the dollar's peso price toward the 455.70-455.80 threshold, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. \par \par \uc2  On debt markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's eight-year PRC bonds were trading to yield 7.33% on an annual basis at the end of the day, compared to the previous session's 7.34% close. \par \par \uc2  --By Felipe Ossa (562) 638 7472 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1801GMT \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6804ve6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
