\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Unchanged; USD Shortage And  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 1998\par 20:44\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso Wednesday ended unchanged against the dollar on a slow trading day as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was held in check on one side by a lack of dollar liquidity and on the other by concern that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in defense of the peso, said a trader with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range between 454.70 pesos and 455.40 pesos to the dollar. One dollar bought 455.00 pesos at the end of trading day, unchanged from the previous day's closing price. \par \par \uc2  The trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, as it had on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  He added that the effective stalemate should continue into tomorrow. "Nothing much will probably happen until after the holidays," the trader said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed on Friday due to the Easter holidays. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On debt markets, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's eight-year PRC bonds were trading\par to yield 7.21% on an annual basis at the end of the day, unchanged from\par a day earlier.\par   --By William Hoke (562) 639 7895\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-04-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1844GMT\par \f28 \par \par 