\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Slightly Weaker Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1998\par 18:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in defense of the Chilean peso, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still ended slightly weaker against the dollar on heavy bank and corporate activity. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range between 439.50 pesos and 442.40 pesos to the dollar. One dollar bought 440.50 pesos at the end of trading day, 50 centavos more than the previous session's closing price. \par \par \uc2  An official with the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but declined to say how many dollars the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold. A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader estimated the figure at around $40 million. \par \par \uc2  'Banks have been buying a lot of dollars in the futures markets recently,' the trader said. 'And those futures purchases have been pushing the spot market higher. Companies have decided they better buy dollars now before the price goes up much more.' \par \par \uc2  The combined weight of bank and business buying forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in, another trader said. 'When the dollar approached 443 (pesos), the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started selling (dollars).' \par \par \uc2  On debt markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's eight-year PRC bonds were trading to yield 6.95% on an annual basis at the end of the day, compared to the previous session's 6.94% close. \par \par \uc2  By William Hoke (562) 639 7895 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1726GMT \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du150014z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
