\par\par \b \uc2  Chile  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  says prepared to sell dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Dec 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and sell dollars to counterbalance any exaggerated drop in the Chilean peso, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Carlos Massad said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market on Thursday, Friday, Tuesday and again on Wednesday to sell dollars as the peso slid near or beyond 440 to a dollar, its lowest level in four years. \par \par \uc2  Massad, who has attributed the peso's sudden slide to shockwaves from the Asian financial crisis and a scarcity of dollars in the local market, declined to estimate how long he expects that lack of liquidity to last. \par \par \uc2  "We don't have a forecast, but we are prepared to face a scarcity (of dollars)," Massad told reporters. "We are more prepared for a scarcity of dollars than an abundance." \par \par \uc2  At around midday Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars with the peso trading at around 438.50, causing it to rise to 436.50, traders said. The dollar had closed at 437.00 pesos on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Massad refused to say how many dollars the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold in previous sessions. According to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders quoted in the Chilean press, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold about $200 million of its reserves since Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Chilean economic officials said this month that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves total about $19 billion and are large enough to fend off any attacks on the peso. \par \par \uc2  Massad also would not say what level the dollar must reach in order to merit the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but traders have speculated the ceiling is 440 pesos. \par \par \uc2  "We prefer that the market form its own opinion about this rather than have the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  give its opinion," he said. \par \par \uc2  Before the Asian crisis started softening the peso in September, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had appreciated about eight percent against the dollar this year, worrying local exporters. \par \par \uc2  ((Tiffany Woods, Santiago newsroom, +562 699-5595 x212)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc301iu2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
