\par\par \b \uc2  Chile Peso Edges Dn Slightly On Dlr; Bond Yields Down \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 1996\par 20:19\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso fell slightly Monday but closed above its session lows on a late round of dollar selling. Bond yields edged down. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, the formal dollar used in trading \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 407.50 pesos, up 0.20 pesos from Friday's close of 407.30, but down from its session highs of 408.40 pesos earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  Dealers Monday said rumors had largely disappeared of imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to widen or even eliminate the trading band in which the dollar trades against the peso. \par \par \uc2  Under the current scheme, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars when the greenback falls below the band's floor, which on Monday stood at 401.98 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Widening the band would ease the pressure for such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is costly in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current high interest rate environment. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, widening the band would allow the dollar to weaken further, pushing up the peso. That would help offset the effects of a recent gas-price hike, by lowering the costs of importing fuel, whose price is denominated in dollars. \par \par \uc2  The gas hike has caused concerns about higher-than-projected monthly inflation in April. \par \par \uc2  But on Monday, the dollar's recent strength internationally helped put slightly more space between the dollar and the floor of its band, though a late round of dollar selling pushed the peso up from its session lows. \par \par \uc2  Among those reportedly selling dollars Monday was state-held Banco del Estado, which dealers on Friday had speculated was purchasing dollars on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 04-22-96 \par \par \uc2  1419EDT \par \par \uc2  1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013ds4m0076p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
