\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Down Against Dollar On Cent Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1995\par 20:11\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (DJ-EMR)--The peso fell against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to cap the rise of the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since October 1994. \par \par \uc2  The formal dollar used for trading \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed up at 373.30/373.80 Wednesday, up 0.50 pesos from Tuesday's close of 372.80/373.30. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began buying small amounts of dollars for pesos around Noon local time (1600 GMT), after the formal dollar used for trading \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a session low bid of near 371 pesos. \par \par \uc2  One trader estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some $15 million from various banks in the market, a relatively small amount. "The effect of its presence in the market was enough" to end the peso's recent rise, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on its open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The peso has strengthened in recent months thanks to the continued strong march of the Chilean economy; indeed, the government is considering a $700 million prepayment of its foreign external debt, according to a newspaper report Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the peso soared Tuesday on news that authorities had jailed brigadier general Pedro Espinoza, one of two former secret police officials convicted of ordering the 1976 assassination of Foreign Minister Orlando Letelier. \par \par \uc2  The government's inability to bring into custody Espinoza and retired general Manuel Contreras -- sentenced to six-year and seven-year sentences, respectively -- spooked local markets in recent days. Contreras remains under military protection in a Navy hospital. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 06-21-95 \par \par \uc2  1411EDT \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011025dr6l005dl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
