\par\par \b \uc2  (WSJ): Chile Counts Mixed Blessings As Peso Rises Versus Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2  By JONATHAN FRIEDLAND \par \uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 1995\par 08:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (AP-DJ)--Buoyed by the country's strong export performance and a surge in foreign direct investment, the Chilean peso rose 11.5% against the dollar in May alone, the Wall Street Journal reports Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But despite calls for relief by exporters and makers of manufactured goods for the domestic market, Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't inclined to brake the peso's rapid rise. \par \par \uc2  Bank officials say that as long as the peso stays within a band calculated against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile's trading partners and designed to keep the country's current-account deficit in check, there's no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively. \par \par \uc2  They note that most of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's major exports, including copper, wood products and even wine, are surging despite the peso's appreciation. Nonetheless, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government of President Eduardo Frei have begun tinkering with exchange-rate policy in recognition of the growing complaints. \par \par \uc2  In the past week, they have modified some of the capital and interest-rate controls credited with shielding Chile from the worst of the Latin American volatility stemming from Mexico's financial crisis, which began in December. \par \par \uc2  In one measure, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped setting interest rates on 90-day government debt and instead began fixing overnight rates. In response, 90-day rates fell to 5.8% from 6.1% in real terms, making the peso less attractive as an investment. \par \par \uc2  The government also allowed private pension funds to invest abroad a bigger percentage of their $2.3 billion in holdings. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-06-95 \par \par \uc2  0600GMT \par \par \uc2  1126 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr66046ip\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (chile near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw)and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority) \cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\cl